```bash
cards "$CARD_ID" shutdown --outcome success
# or
cards "$CARD_ID" shutdown --outcome blocked --message "waiting on review"
# or
cards "$CARD_ID" shutdown --outcome error --message "what failed"
```

`--outcome` defaults to `success`; `--message` is optional free text. Exit 0 confirms durable request acceptance, not that cleanup has completed.

<%= it.variant({
  "claude-code": "Do not make any later tool call after the shutdown command. Delivery is not completion: the runtime records one terminal decision, and the execution wrapper reports containment and output finalization after stopping its owned processes.\n\n4. End the session cleanly. The execution wrapper owns termination in response to the accepted decision — no separate kill commands are needed.\n",
